cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Keel, cite the repository."
title: "Keel: checkpoint-level misalignment drift detection for open-weight models"
abstract: >-
  Keel scans an open-weight checkpoint against a reference on a fixed probe panel
  and reports a paired drift vector, an internal misalignment cosine, and a
  causally validated set of MLP units responsible for the drift. It supports a
  black-box channel over the Meta Model API and a white-box channel over Meta
  open weights.
authors:
  - name: "cptlight"
    alias: "cptlight"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TCPCore/keel"
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - interpretability
  - open-weights
  - misalignment
